<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine gov't to appeal airport ruling-agency.</title>
<headline>Argentine gov't to appeal airport ruling-agency.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine government will formally ask the Supreme Court Wednesday to overall a judge's ruling against plans to privatize most of the country's airports, the private DyN news agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>No government spokesman was immediately available to comment on the report, but government advisor Jorge Rottemberg said July 8 that the government would appeal the ruling by Judge Liliana Heiland.</p>
<p>Rottemberg said that the privatization would not be delayed by Heiland's ruling the same day that a presidential decree authorizing the sell-off was void.</p>
<p>President Carlos Menem finally approved the airport privatization in June, and the government intends to seek bids for a single, 30-year concession to be awarded in October.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
